lld: --enable-non-contiguous-regions crashed now and then (about one link in
64) in OutputSection::finalizeInputSections(): the merge synthetic section
took its potential spill list with try_emplace(syn, it->second), and when
that insertion grew potentialSpillLists' DenseMap, it->second pointed into
the freed buckets. Copy the list before inserting.

Upstream: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/245888 (drop this
patch once a release has the fix).

--- a/lld/ELF/OutputSections.cpp	2026-11-25 17:34:51.646205287 +0900
+++ b/lld/ELF/OutputSections.cpp	2026-11-25 19:01:17.966527396 +0900
@@ -244,10 +244,13 @@
         syn->entsize = ms->entsize;
         isd->sections.push_back(syn);
         // The merge synthetic section inherits the potential spill locations of
-        // its first contained section.
+        // its first contained section. Copy the list first: try_emplace may
+        // grow the map and free the bucket that it->second refers to.
         auto it = script->potentialSpillLists.find(ms);
-        if (it != script->potentialSpillLists.end())
-          script->potentialSpillLists.try_emplace(syn, it->second);
+        if (it != script->potentialSpillLists.end()) {
+          LinkerScript::PotentialSpillList list = it->second;
+          script->potentialSpillLists.try_emplace(syn, list);
+        }
       }
       (*i)->addSection(ms);
     }
